QE = {1: "Now the use of this path, our present subject, is set forth.", 2: "Thus this whole path, as it rests in consciousness, through that rests also in void, intellect, breath, channel-wheels, and bodies.", 3: "And outside too, everywhere in liṅga, image, fire, altar and the rest; so it stands, whole and part-wise, in sequence and all at once.", 4: "Laid out from consciousness-principle to the outer, this path: at each level one should make one's own form shine, by own freedom, in fitting form.", 5: "And everything's form everywhere — even his does not not shine; for we cannot bear exclusion anywhere, even in dream.", 6: "Thus one should behold the body as filled with the universe-path, painted by time's activity — the abode of pulsation made of space and time.", 7: "So beheld, he is made of the deities within the universe; to be meditated, worshipped, libated — entered then, one is freed.", 8: "Thus pot, cloth, liṅga, altar, book, water — or whatever one may see anywhere: there one should reach identity-with-that.", 9: "Therein offering of things is held worship through non-difference; and contemplation of full-formedness is called meditation.", 10: "Unshaking contemplation of fullness brings firmness; and through inner-mutter practice, reflecting, one becomes a mantra-vessel.", 11: "Effecting the melting of self-difference of the beings offered therein, their ray-rich being he should bestow — devoted to the fire-rite.", 12: "For one so acting, seeing all with equal eye, unwaveringness is the pure vow — evenness taught in the Nandiśikhā.", 13: "Thus through worship, japa, meditation, fire-offering, vow, and rule in sequence, the ancients called the complete state absorption.", 14: "Here in worship, japa and the rest, whether outward or inward, there is no rule at all about materials, nor any prohibition.", 15: "No use here whatsoever for visualization, purification, twilight-rites and the rest; and in the Trika Sūtra it is said sacrifice arises toward the rite.", 16: "Not knowing rule, knowing rule, and 'thus' and so on at length: when, as, by which, where one's own consciousness is gracious.", 17: "Then, so, by that, there: each respective enjoyable — and that is the rule; all, worldly and unworldly, one should employ here by that.", 18: "In steadiness: but the trembler should forcibly diminish tremor — by force, as, by whatever means, in sequence or all at once, or.", 19: "Doubt melts within — so he should become striving; the goddesses resting in mind, rite, and senses he should libate with forbidden things indeed.", 20: "And the hero-vow one should salute — thus the Bhargaśikhā word: for doubt is impurity, weariness, contraction — thus this.", 21: "Inside the world-prison it forges gross-post shackles; mantras are letter-natured, substance five-elemented.", 22: "The breathing kind which is consciousness-selfed — where is mixture there, how? With mixture absent, what is this doubt — even hers clearly baseless.", 23: "One should not doubt; thus doubt dissolves through disregard — in the Sarvācāra, Vīrālī, Niśācara, Krama and the rest.", 24: "And this is spread in the śāstras — there it is said: for from doubt arises weariness, from doubt being a vessel of obstacles.", 25: "And said Utpaladeva, the venerable guru of my guru: the all-doubt thunderbolt path — we bow to the Māheśvara path.", 26: "For attaining the anuttara state, this āṇava with means shown at great length — indeed, make it grow, O wise ones!"}


def main() -> None:
    spans = source_spans('tantraloka-a12')
    assert {int(k): v for k, v in TOK.items()} == {k: v for k, v in spans.items()}, 'TOKENS DRIFT'
    assert all(len(TOK[v]) == len(CM[v]) == len(GLOSS[v]) for v in TOK), 'ROW DRIFT'
    json.dump({str(k): v for k, v in TOK.items()}, open('tantraloka-a12/cm/spans-tal-a12.json', 'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
    cm = {}
    for v in TOK:
        cm[str(v)] = [[CM[v][i][0], CM[v][i][1], CM[v][i][2]] for i in range(len(TOK[v]))]
    json.dump(cm, open('tantraloka-a12/cm/l0cm-v1-26.json', 'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
    t1 = [{"verse_id": "tal-a12-v%02d" % v, "song": "tal-a12", "verse": v, "quick_english": QE[v], "quick_english_source": "manual", "tokens": [{"surface": TOK[v][i], "quick_gloss": GLOSS[v][i]} for i in range(len(TOK[v]))]} for v in sorted(TOK)]
    json.dump(t1, open('tantraloka-a12/working-t1-tal-a12.json', 'w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)
    md = '# Tantraloka-a12 — T1\n*Source: GRETIL tantraloka (KSTS) via workcfg taloka. Span-exact vs source_spans. Machine-proposed, needs human review.*\n'
    for v in sorted(TOK):
        md += '\n\n## tal-a12-v%02d\n' % v
        md += ' '.join('[and]-%s (%s)' % (GLOSS[v][i], TOK[v][i]) for i in range(len(TOK[v]))) + ' // %d //\n' % v
    open('tantraloka-a12/T1-tal-a12.md', 'w').write(md)
    print('cm+t1 written, verses:', len(t1), 'tokens:', sum(len(x) for x in TOK.values()))


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
